From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] phone-rpc: support bounded registry renames

Run75 completed the bounded observation window with no write-mode refusals but
the DSP repeatedly called method33 (frename), which was unimplemented.

Turn the fixed four-entry store into a bounded copy-on-write registry namespace.
Only file basenames below the exact persist sensor registry directory and the
exact camera registry dump are admitted. Names are canonicalized, relative
registry basenames are accepted, traversal and other prefixes are refused.

The store now holds up to512 in-memory files,16MiB aggregate capacity,1MiB per
file and64 handles. Rename is atomic inside RAM, preserves open handles to the
source and refuses to replace a destination with an active handle. No host
descriptor or pathname is writable, and deinitialization releases every file.

Wire tests cover method33, cross-path readback and rename-back. Storage tests
cover canonical names, replacement and active-destination refusal. These checks
do not qualify phone writes or a sensor stream.

